ServiceNow for Cowork

Maintained adaptation by Lior Kamrat of
https://github.com/fizamusthafa/servicenow-cowork-plugin
Upstream baseline: 05c37c3.

The upstream MIT license and its original copyright notice are preserved
verbatim in LICENSE. The adaptation restricts the connection to four read-only
tools, adds bounded incident discovery, and provides portable packaging.

The color icon restores plugin/color.png byte-for-byte from upstream baseline
05c37c3 (Git blob 711cbf5054e2e7082e9dd42ff740ec599cb5c0d2).
The white/transparent 32px outline derives from the same baseline's outline.png
(Git blob f47d3b913c0e09f3f1db8f8feb3b6ffb3eb41728), without redrawing or resizing.
Its navy background (3,45,66) and green mark (117,191,80) were separated by
projecting each RGB pixel onto that color vector, clamping coverage to [0,1],
and multiplying the original alpha by coverage. RGB is white throughout.
scripts/icons.js verifies both reviewed assets without overwriting either.
No Microsoft logo is included.
ServiceNow and Microsoft product names identify the systems this project
connects to. This project is not an official product of either company.

Dependency licenses are supplied by their respective npm packages. Dependencies
are restored with npm ci and are not vendored in the source or plugin archives.
